#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128986 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d342be-ebaf-5e94-b641-ea8ce6f14c12" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type I Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "9cbb7321-753d-5253-8b64-072e3cc227bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-6101" :question/problem "![](images/76/766a7abf73e9f9ef85164b1165166d7493cd36cdc75d0f244e475fed8aeea8fd.png)\n\nRepresent the type I region above using set notation." :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: a \\leq x  \\leq b, \\quad g(x) \\leq y \\leq f(x) \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x.$\n\n- The curve $x=y-1$ can be written as $y=x+1.$\n\n- The curve $y=7-x$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=1$ and $x=3.$ So, we have $1 \\leq x \\leq 3.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x)$. A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](images/ac/acf870e74a9029543a6e6b21995c293f67f251b54dfad9584220780bc3a0b454.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=x+1$ and leaves through the upper function $y=7-x.$ So, we have $x+1 \\leq y \\leq 7-x.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD= \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\: x+1 \\leq y \\leq 7-x \\big\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128987 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85335de6-e1dc-5a2f-b30a-806627759030" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type II Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "cce0a7b2-7b25-5da6-8aa2-cbe8a40cd522" :question/math-academy-id "e-6102" :question/problem "![](images/39/3919a6a8442e983a9ca3465b2ed9abbeda18b7dc8d21b7c74b1851b53c1be714.png)\n\nRepresent the type II region above using set notation." :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: a \\leq y  \\leq b, \\quad g(y) \\leq x \\leq f(y) \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y.$\n\n- The curve $y = 2-x^2$ can be written as $x = -\\sqrt{2-y}.$ Note that we have picked the negative square root since $x\\leq 0$ in our region.\n\n- The curve $x=\\dfrac{y-2}{2}$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=-2$ and $y=2.$ So, we have $-2 \\leq y \\leq 2.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y)$. A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/0c/0cf258d0269db0977d5c19fe7abd159f13319bb493394fbd049e5660d88a1d6f.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=-\\sqrt{2-y}$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\dfrac{y-2}{2}.$ So, we have $-\\sqrt{2-y} \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{y-2}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD= \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: -\\sqrt{2-y} \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{y-2}{2} \\bigg\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128988 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/id #uuid "cd9ce5bf-1663-5110-8aaa-8f0f47d7d30a" :question/math-academy-id "e-6103" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=x^2$ and the line $y=4?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\ny=x^2\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx = \\pm\\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/59/59d32c44bae848d52adc188e15a8bab470b3eccd887cad45c231b66c486284fc.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: x^2 \\leq y \\leq 4 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 4, \\: -\\sqrt{y} \\leq x \\leq \\sqrt{y} \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d342be-ebaf-5e94-b641-ea8ce6f14c12" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04649150-61a8-5e98-810a-59f23d047e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573427} {:answer/id #uuid "565b5291-ae6b-5a1c-807b-942f6bde746d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b0/b07159c516c62a8b063c23bdea55198d8a93be291d52aaaa9f9d5f85ed713d38.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573532} {:answer/id #uuid "7f1dd8db-1d39-55ed-955b-d094c405cd18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8f65df619adf0fa46b447ad93fa1527c9b64a456f8244ed218bb01d763422d39.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573589} {:answer/id #uuid "8f610be9-7b4f-5feb-9545-049ae6ad3321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/70142ba52b7ed0194952276c5d952b67b71326b8525ca0a5b9fe4e7ad8fdb038.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573608} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a8910b-c256-5c84-9abe-5538a63aa0a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/aa/aa15ae13bab07a98408e47248cb311c8a2f66947457b44fb6d84bd531b78e890.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f1dd8db-1d39-55ed-955b-d094c405cd18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8f65df619adf0fa46b447ad93fa1527c9b64a456f8244ed218bb01d763422d39.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573589} :answer-field/id #uuid "137bad3a-0a18-596a-af7e-6e522a905519" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fda2de1-9ece-56ec-9887-95ffd8614a09" :question/math-academy-id "q-168112" :question/problem "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](images/fc/fc79eeb10b320beb24a54e3cbbbaf8b539fc0c51cb9f6f8ac8127b6faeca1180.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85335de6-e1dc-5a2f-b30a-806627759030" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e353de59-45ed-5d3e-a3c7-c62ccb8bfee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/32e6ed07f3229c8e6016d12dd35c42597888662fbc909f53bc07e495a73958e8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389596} {:answer/id #uuid "189f5878-608c-523c-8af3-61b336e7fea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389597} {:answer/id #uuid "cae29720-9bdf-5675-b7dc-87fb52dc9fc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/36/36275eef6e634c83c614626bc2af6b97cd5bafddc8c02b64ba2a1aa7ea983317.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389598} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e89d64-16cb-5f6e-924f-288db18c0bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/de643820e7690a10eae2e7de2e2cb974700996b36130af4f45c446640b49dcc4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389599} {:answer/id #uuid "a2e82089-b886-5a96-8c4e-a2c7d256121e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5a/5ac45c6757e187796674ca4beda4ff73c60835b401df302bfd8a91fa5c98b68c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6e89d64-16cb-5f6e-924f-288db18c0bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/de/de643820e7690a10eae2e7de2e2cb974700996b36130af4f45c446640b49dcc4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389599} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e761f31-f26b-54c2-90ef-d2fbb7506ab7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2da77bc4-04e1-56ef-a7c8-2c62ea7852fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-168140" :question/problem "Which of the following is a type II region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/1b/1bee7870760a7c267ca83806f04b3fa8b933891fa5e5524ce76ee09f2c7c98e0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284608 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cd755d6-ee26-5605-9cbe-f442f026bcb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465567} {:answer/id #uuid "90d1f970-eed0-567b-adf3-4c7f5db4de6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d1f970-eed0-567b-adf3-4c7f5db4de6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465568} :answer-field/id #uuid "b24e7b72-59ed-526f-b9bb-99fa8de74857" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466627} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c5e733d-2645-53d4-b251-1052eb9bfd88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465569} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e920b2-5a83-5a7d-a18e-45c6f18042ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0e920b2-5a83-5a7d-a18e-45c6f18042ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465570} :answer-field/id #uuid "968f8407-a641-5c7b-bd5c-8fca908630cf" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466628} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53e90f41-9954-53ce-b5e3-a689609a8831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465571} {:answer/id #uuid "cfdf9afc-37c6-5c72-9786-1c95a9f10540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53e90f41-9954-53ce-b5e3-a689609a8831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465571} :answer-field/id #uuid "95f001d0-6e52-56f5-a0ec-26fc887a3762" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0adcc01-b22f-5ba4-864b-30820cc15f4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-168841" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the triangle bounded between the lines $y=1-x,$ $y=x-1,$ and $x=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=1-x\\, & ⟹\\,x=1-y \\\\ y=x-1\\, & ⟹\\,x=y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/27/27503f983e3e02fa748bb8ef32966a6cd3b5fff29082ffaf3c10d0521b630e93.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x-1\\le y\\le 1-x\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1-|y|\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4564e18e-6dd3-592f-b9bf-6a20676a3b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472766} {:answer/id #uuid "45b0e7fa-80cd-5a12-9738-58511f6045e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4564e18e-6dd3-592f-b9bf-6a20676a3b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472766} :answer-field/id #uuid "855b803a-41ec-54c7-b217-cd7e07f3f903" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90203ed1-4476-519f-9f88-b4e02ca64ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472768} {:answer/id #uuid "97ba8073-07f2-57a8-a1bd-4281e7eb3559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90203ed1-4476-519f-9f88-b4e02ca64ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472768} :answer-field/id #uuid "193ec04e-372e-5547-a37c-6dcc99f24e8b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cec72ac9-8abf-5d07-936d-25ec93cb55c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472770} {:answer/id #uuid "1f3c4534-d68b-508f-9b49-1132a3559fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f3c4534-d68b-508f-9b49-1132a3559fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472771} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa6603a-92f4-51b4-90a0-db5e275129ca" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fd6f7437-bc45-50cb-9400-bcd422c5b408" :question/math-academy-id "q-168921" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/bc/bc6b71d1fe69abd34dbd939dc62ede5201b75713e25456cf084e889bc44f449e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.4$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/4a/4a1fd7069abaa3b3fa4d9c286773d226798bf3ad565e85663cab44557fd635c1.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=-1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/26/260e8e959ca95a029a98bd4102106a66df418ea73c0640398c8fdebfdbf812f6.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85335de6-e1dc-5a2f-b30a-806627759030" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86e11a1f-00dc-51de-8fae-8e31288e9455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515155} {:answer/id #uuid "98af0664-fef3-5195-8942-4ae62f79f459" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515196} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3d9aa4-b230-5307-8b9e-8fda1b89d36a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 3\\,,\\,2x\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515211} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a1af78-5337-58fe-9506-fb9b3db058f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 2\\,,\\,2x\\le y\\le (x-1)^{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515222} {:answer/id #uuid "f038c740-7bd9-542c-aa85-3c158363caa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f038c740-7bd9-542c-aa85-3c158363caa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515376} :answer-field/id #uuid "121eed80-0cfa-5e17-b370-61189884e2ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "771776cb-495a-5541-85ae-ed89a3b38002" :question/math-academy-id "q-71830" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f7a556f986c44b922908b79e3982e098eb7250d9d470092ba2c45bbffe190913.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny=2x\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2}\n$$\n\nThe function $x=\\sqrt{y}+1$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=4.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le 4.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/c5/c55d5f809462b767122ccc4af97c5b4d243730ed24f655bdc18e35ec57e25ce2.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=\\frac{y}{2}$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\sqrt{y}+1.$ So, we have $\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d342be-ebaf-5e94-b641-ea8ce6f14c12" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2ddc4b0-74ef-5d8b-9bdf-ce18a05a7898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fa/fa55dd7b6de34bb33f43d59978eb211a1c2f78bfcf2f9e726f5a9e5c967fef1f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393189} {:answer/id #uuid "67b7dda0-a5cf-50c4-972e-b6cfbf49f53a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b2/b23dac6004f438e6705187b5fda2cb4034eeac5d70bcfb95a31ac8f1ca41c700.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393190} {:answer/id #uuid "1997a5ab-e4a8-5279-85db-659d59bc9902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393191} {:answer/id #uuid "23dc4607-d3fe-5ae5-825e-486ea309f487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/22/225e79155fe769efb2273d5063fce38ce305ae25a11a0276e505b08420da790a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393192} {:answer/id #uuid "bacb1889-6272-5be5-98cb-ea6bda35386a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4d/4d92f7a616ce7908ecbcf2b8c32104aa348067014923377c1b692f9deaf9302f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23dc4607-d3fe-5ae5-825e-486ea309f487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/22/225e79155fe769efb2273d5063fce38ce305ae25a11a0276e505b08420da790a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393192} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8f92f31-fa93-53be-abd0-258a50093ab8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8a8de6a-3043-5d0c-ae35-56392ae16ec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72038" :question/problem "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](images/af/af08994008c1df01d052fbc345e6892fed33b7d82ad2de5eb55089e9a879e602.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d342be-ebaf-5e94-b641-ea8ce6f14c12" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ad9fabe-6ac2-5a64-ad33-5fdd7127093f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429963} {:answer/id #uuid "1d70f350-c29f-598f-92ec-fbca126bbc5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/78/781f679784282a55e4ff6b7a5537047ef2f45c8346cc9d1ed341407ecb8f8a38.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429964} {:answer/id #uuid "52b32bb1-058f-52fc-8bbd-90d501685805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ba/ba9994e94193fb25ac13c50e22e17c571ef563420325a02b593a37c4634e3998.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429965} {:answer/id #uuid "795e2b60-0fa8-5665-b329-1cbd1b3e42fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/69de9afdd158f32add63cc93e37b12ed0e3a80fcb5b1cb04cb88fb493c9ca723.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429967} {:answer/id #uuid "b347940c-aaa8-5068-a270-5cc37376373d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/70662d02852c7299ab1c040362664de79de8bc51689b0611796f63a737412693.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "795e2b60-0fa8-5665-b329-1cbd1b3e42fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/69de9afdd158f32add63cc93e37b12ed0e3a80fcb5b1cb04cb88fb493c9ca723.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429967} :answer-field/id #uuid "e615de10-cf5a-5071-a58d-94a8d37e22e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "033e3725-7b31-599b-85d8-6c6f830b966d" :question/math-academy-id "q-72042" :question/problem "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](images/00/00654c32dbc74614de9b6fdd0f39a5f7d4ecb6ccca0c642ab7ca4a2a8cfe1d89.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d342be-ebaf-5e94-b641-ea8ce6f14c12" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9db76155-8671-5467-8f85-0d2112f29767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-(x-1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375309} {:answer/id #uuid "157b2c25-5099-5a77-a1cb-81b2c8477282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-(x-1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375310} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed955ce-ddd7-5600-92b9-fa5809520e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le \\sqrt{3-y}+1,\\,2\\le y\\le 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375311} {:answer/id #uuid "a5af797e-ba24-5523-92e5-1255fde9881a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le (x-1)^{2}+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375312} {:answer/id #uuid "46705277-fd7c-564a-b8ea-f2c9d078002b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le \\sqrt{3-y}+1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "157b2c25-5099-5a77-a1cb-81b2c8477282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-(x-1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375310} :answer-field/id #uuid "e789573f-de55-535f-afca-3eee3bb4aa74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "76027899-49f4-5ed4-93bc-de501abde637" :question/math-academy-id "q-72124" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d1c2f0e830c6d3beca27886e839816f46a00be322c9d7cff18248d118ed0e617.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type I region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{3-y}+1\\,⟹\\,y=3-(x-1)^{2}\n$$\n\nThe function $y=0$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=1$ and $x=2.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](images/be/be799df2140d3a437bb311427dcae0e297cb6bd3844f88932157eb6ace6e7e59.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=0$ and leaves through the upper function $y=3-(x-1)^{2}.$ So, we have $0\\le y\\le 3-(x-1)^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-(x-1)^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85335de6-e1dc-5a2f-b30a-806627759030" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "346f4b41-4357-55ec-ac31-99d9a84feeb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2(x-1)^{3}+1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336524} {:answer/id #uuid "461f0e90-3bc0-5f56-a6a0-7316a35b85c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2(x-1)^{3}+1,\\,1\\le x\\le 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336683} {:answer/id #uuid "5b7fd321-2e22-5929-997a-7aac95e1bcfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336863} {:answer/id #uuid "bea653c2-d7f7-5c76-aaa8-8eefa8f3ec56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337726} {:answer/id #uuid "f653d3d8-54d3-5454-b6e5-c9af87eee1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bea653c2-d7f7-5c76-aaa8-8eefa8f3ec56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337726} :answer-field/id #uuid "17659af0-1ac9-5a42-9e47-a7cf0ab901c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7dd69b50-459c-5dc4-905d-619404665111" :question/math-academy-id "q-72140" :question/problem "![](images/c7/c72f0a6f9bfb83be34cf911d2a2a18b04a40f92f4d1f6c065b9d6f03f56301b6.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny=2(x-1)^{3}+1\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1\n$$\n\nThe function $x=0$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=3.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/1d/1dcfc91a9392998f6de0e4ede2e67d9487f71bb521adad024c3c6891b56d0163.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=0$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y-1}{2}}+1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406982 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b532929-031f-53ba-845b-1b69f35ae5ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473278} {:answer/id #uuid "da5ae196-6ddc-5f90-8faf-ce02251fa644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da5ae196-6ddc-5f90-8faf-ce02251fa644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473279} :answer-field/id #uuid "8261d6df-4d7c-5438-ab24-46a9a778e5ea" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474034} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff2626a4-af3b-558c-898b-e325dcd7c8a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473280} {:answer/id #uuid "74014f19-619f-54ff-9fc7-8f16f269680a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74014f19-619f-54ff-9fc7-8f16f269680a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473281} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f34c2c1-88e7-5e59-bf72-b638136d3b12" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474035} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d131820-9e7d-5679-bbf5-8ff122bec3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473282} {:answer/id #uuid "38a132f3-eea1-5c88-b25c-151a9517cd9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d131820-9e7d-5679-bbf5-8ff122bec3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473282} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f148b1b-a08c-5f92-88d7-fab284af6a47" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d779a1b-dcae-59f0-822c-7860f9483ab7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72160" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y=\\sqrt[3]{x},$ in the first quadrant?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{3}\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y} \\\\ y=\\sqrt[3]{x}\\, & ⟹\\,x={y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/89/899357795c6d5b81d3cb619d71493ad787645697fe1f2fcecda78c1b875f388e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{x}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{3}\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cb3d1e7-cf6a-54b2-a095-b9fdc68a8d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467926} {:answer/id #uuid "cab149b0-2702-528d-b56e-23d4232647f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cab149b0-2702-528d-b56e-23d4232647f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467927} :answer-field/id #uuid "368ddd66-9d80-586f-9e2a-9ab70f075343" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468684} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ea3c229-904d-5a2f-8d07-a00dada077bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467928} {:answer/id #uuid "7d445f31-2d12-5062-a2a4-99e2b64c0491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ea3c229-904d-5a2f-8d07-a00dada077bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467928} :answer-field/id #uuid "4edea166-3bfd-535f-b98e-b624be2d49a5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a94e95bb-c951-576f-aa60-7b79a87fb894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467930} {:answer/id #uuid "1541c926-bd73-5e47-854d-d4e15738f59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a94e95bb-c951-576f-aa60-7b79a87fb894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467930} :answer-field/id #uuid "88bc4663-71c0-5111-9c92-a5bd0ddc37dc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f581ab20-43e5-59a8-ac58-914378a7361e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72186" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ and the line $y=2-|x|?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/6f/6f35161e7efbd53c9ef558ffe88d8e046771128965a9fdd02143ae37a9b130ea.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,2-|x|\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/76/769a521cd6b05ecf05052da382e40295b26be66fe56e4eff7c6940c9032f2f0b.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93784bc3-b560-52b9-a35d-2ec831b381f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467932} {:answer/id #uuid "3e4ef645-0e9e-59ca-9ead-4e534938e7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93784bc3-b560-52b9-a35d-2ec831b381f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467932} :answer-field/id #uuid "fae03209-445f-57ef-a7d8-bf499239612a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea766b7-5902-5718-9a79-ebd9d7790d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467934} {:answer/id #uuid "652141fa-413d-505f-be84-3dff8c027c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fea766b7-5902-5718-9a79-ebd9d7790d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467934} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1a093da-8121-5419-baa0-42398a34c5c0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38c7e8b2-4b4c-577e-a27a-0aa07ff9fbc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467936} {:answer/id #uuid "482c64c9-5eab-5414-829d-60978c25b3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "482c64c9-5eab-5414-829d-60978c25b3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467937} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7660e82-ac96-5396-b514-daa03b2886a3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b03842bf-e94f-5526-903d-de5a2a3bccca" :question/math-academy-id "q-72187" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/28/28290c5530efd27a979f4284481ca7e0384342d7d426dde0ab36894a0d77a166.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.5$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/30/3007cffb725faee44d2a06ad077eec630791b1a94c373a323f62d0d721c87207.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.5$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/38/383f88668435556d3a856cf852caf548b1f1bf3a90d50f9d85d7968188984804.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186429975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85335de6-e1dc-5a2f-b30a-806627759030" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177be529-dbfe-5550-a65b-a03b4c722a7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le {e}^{x-1},\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429962} {:answer/id #uuid "69b6c086-4549-55a7-9eba-d0041a274109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429966} {:answer/id #uuid "ad13df4f-7bd9-5a03-86d7-02175fdb12da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429968} {:answer/id #uuid "c5dacd0b-ebeb-5ba4-b6db-4ab0dd2f71e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le {e}^{x-1},\\,1\\le x\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429970} {:answer/id #uuid "dfdb17ab-530e-5006-a6b1-b68bfc5121a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le {e}^{x-1},\\,0\\le x\\le 2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69b6c086-4549-55a7-9eba-d0041a274109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429966} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1839b45-678e-5716-ac62-7bfdda74ad68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5cace0f5-d8d3-5cc8-93c4-64d577bf2d3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-72344" :question/problem "![](images/40/4066b07ace047e9a7ce813ed70dd6648649a192d648ed810fa96b5146d2c5581.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny={e}^{x-1}\\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\n$$\n\nThe function $x=0$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=e.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le e.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/68/680842905f6e308d3c438063769bde9854401a300371452d1c0735bb7d272a02.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=0$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)+1\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d342be-ebaf-5e94-b641-ea8ce6f14c12" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type I Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42fce8a9-744e-501b-b63d-929131e43c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}+3\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339714} {:answer/id #uuid "48f05eeb-6c69-5082-9394-5aa453de3a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339780} {:answer/id #uuid "83a796cb-2ed0-536b-8594-c2a20a39138f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}+1\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340312} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b5b4fc-cc9b-5f82-8152-ccb743f12fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340650} {:answer/id #uuid "f28f1294-f1d6-5a5b-95ff-68c8e657614f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-{x}^{2}+3\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83a796cb-2ed0-536b-8594-c2a20a39138f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}+1\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340312} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec358aec-5fab-5c06-8165-7a3899689ed9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341802}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec05fcbc-74be-5268-b887-7ddc7e9fb51a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73532" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d69e6b6550f7e4cae0785daaa19c0a52382a595c40309dccd1d832dbc6d2f82f.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type I region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{y-1}+1\\,⟹\\,y=(x-1)^{2}+1\n$$\n\nThe function $y=-(x-1)^{2}+3$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=1$ and $x=2.$ So, we have $1\\le x\\le 2.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](images/94/942a39f885e6f88bef997e27914d05359be86ae1d6204f3834f0829ce4b81136.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=(x-1)^{2}+1$ and leaves through the upper function $y=-(x-1)^{2}+3.$ So, we have $(x-1)^{2}+1\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}+1\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85335de6-e1dc-5a2f-b30a-806627759030" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1756c48c-665f-5f06-b577-1b909cc87f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+3\\le x\\le \\frac{y}{2}+2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514921} {:answer/id #uuid "1a8d8801-ef97-55e2-bc3a-31cf1be29d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\sqrt{y}\\le y\\le \\frac{y}{2},\\,1\\le x\\le 3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514930} {:answer/id #uuid "a8039587-077a-5341-9003-3971e08c6ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515225} {:answer/id #uuid "b4fa72f4-3cd9-588c-8d31-a887a4ecafd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le y\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3,\\,1\\le x\\le 3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515251} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ff3e83-5d71-5daa-b2f8-25c47f45a202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le 2.5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8039587-077a-5341-9003-3971e08c6ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515225} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dd26fe5-df42-54f1-a759-c32dddc997da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80f56e91-1777-5d7a-b918-7d315f6b332a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73534" :question/problem "![](images/c3/c316b62d5c1a08c6513413fd87c36c6feb26fb632709909a9c9f761d0806c4af.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-2(x-3)\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{y}{2}+3\n$$\n\nThe function $x=-\\sqrt{y}+2$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=3.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/fb/fb05eec73599c1beb8dd588c478208315f6edaf10af999115eb29fa10d5601e9.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=-\\sqrt{y}+2$ and leaves through the upper function $x=-\\frac{y}{2}+3.$ So, we have $-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3\\}.\n$$"}]}
